{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false},"description":"Compares two local executables (base_path and target_path, both absolute; optional Mach-O slice applied to both; max_list 1-5000, default 500) and returns a by-name structural diff. Reports base and target identity (path, sha256, bytes), the target subject, identical, format_changed (base/target format family), size_delta, entry_point_changed (virtual addresses), and added/removed imports (library+name+ordinal), exports (name+ordinal), libraries and sections, per-section Shannon-entropy deltas for sections present in both, and inferred hardening_changes (ELF PIE/RELRO/NX/stack-canary/FORTIFY/stripped; PE DYNAMIC_BASE/NX/HIGH_ENTROPY_VA/GUARD_CF/FORCE_INTEGRITY/NO_SEH/Authenticode; Mach-O PIE/stack-exec/code-signature/encryption/restrict). Every list is bounded with its own coverage. It does NOT unpack, detect renames (a rename is one removal plus one addition), evaluate signature trust, or recover code or behavior. Both files are read once (<=256 MiB each) through the stable-snapshot reader and parsed in-process; neither file is run, and no network or temporary files are used; the complete report is capped at 8 MiB with a typed resource error if exceeded. A side that is not ELF/PE/Mach-O yields empty structural lists and a limitation, indicators that do not apply to a format are null, and any truncation is reported in that list's coverage.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"examples":[{"base_path":"/artifacts/application-v1","target_path":"/artifacts/application-v2"},{"base_path":"/artifacts/application-arm64-old","max_list":100,"slice":"arm64","target_path":"/artifacts/application-arm64-new"}],"properties":{"base_path":{"description":"Absolute path to the baseline (older) executable","minLength":1,"pattern":"^[^\\x00]*$","type":"string"},"max_list":{"default":500,"description":"L